scripts/daily_diary.sh now prints its own per-run spend on stderr, and the diary on stdout is unchanged. It's in two commits: ecf15eee is the script, committed before any verification or cargo run as the plan required, and 8c30a63e is the ARCHITECTURE.md entry. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and cargo test all pass with 0 failures; no Rust was touched.

I did one thing differently from the spec, and why. The spec said to capture the run's output and grep it for the ↳ usage line. That can't work here. Stdin is a file, and src/cli.rs turns on quiet mode when stdin and stdout are both non-terminals. Piping stdout into tee makes that true, and quiet mode suppresses print_usage, so the captured file would never contain the ↳ line. It would also silently take colour and chrome away from anyone running the script in a terminal.

So stdout is left alone, and the spend comes from the "type":"usage" record that yoyo writes to .yoyo/audit.jsonl whether or not quiet is on. The script finds it in this run's new audit lines. That pattern matches 28 real records in the live audit file.

Test output. I ran a stub YOYO_BIN against the block copied out of the shipped file with sed, each case in its own temp dir, all in one command:
```
(a) exit=0  Spend (this run): {"cost_usd":0.0123,"input_tokens":1000,"output_tokens":200,"type":"usage"}
            Spend audit: 2 record(s) this run (line 0 → 2); 91 bytes cumulative in .yoyo/audit.jsonl
(b) exit=124  Spend (this run): no usage record — the process did not reach its terminal emit (no_terminal_emit)
              Spend audit: 1 record(s) this run (line 0 → 1); 16 bytes cumulative in .yoyo/audit.jsonl
(c) exit=0  … no_terminal_emit
            Spend audit: WARNING — no .yoyo/audit.jsonl; audit records were not written this run (cumulative size unknown)
(d) exit=0  Spend (this run): {"cost_usd":0.5,"type":"usage"}
            Spend audit: 2 record(s) this run (line 5 → 7); 128 bytes cumulative in .yoyo/audit.jsonl
(e) new exit=0 old exit=0 — stdout BYTE-IDENTICAL to pre-change (41 bytes), both honest absences on stderr
(f) exit-3 run: new exit=3 old exit=3
```
Case (e) was the unchanged-diary check: YOYO_AUDIT unset, no audit file, no usage record, and cmp against the old script's stdout. The exit status matches the old script in every case.

Side effect. The temporary prompt file used to be left behind when yoyo failed. It's now deleted, and the non-zero exit code is still passed on.

Possible bug in last session's `social.sh` change. It greps for the same ↳ line, and it too reads stdin from a file and pipes output through tee. By the same reasoning that grep probably never matches in production, so it would always print no_terminal_emit. I got this from reading the code and haven't seen it on a real social run. Its audit-count half isn't affected. I left it alone because it's outside this task's files, and noted it in ARCHITECTURE.md as a follow-up.

What this doesn't fix. It's a per-run report, not a permanent record: if the runner's checkout is thrown away, the number goes with it. A permanent record would have to live in a workflow file, which is protected and needs a human. Because of the sub-agent token issue (yologdev/yoagent#173), every number here is a lower bound. dream.sh and synthesize.yml still report no spend at all.
